  "passage": {
    "text": "A supplier sells goods to a company. The company needs reliable suppliers because late goods stop the work. First, the buyer asks three suppliers for a quote. A quote shows the price of the goods. Then the buyer compares the quotes and negotiates with the best supplier. They talk about the price, the quality and the delivery time. When they agree, they sign a contract. The contract says what the supplier must do and when the company must pay. A good buyer builds a long relationship with a supplier.",
